{"id":4727,"date":"2026-03-30T15:21:38","date_gmt":"2026-03-30T14:21:38","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4727"},"modified":"2026-03-30T15:26:07","modified_gmt":"2026-03-30T14:26:07","slug":"from-the-ground-up-dig-into-their-first-co-design-with-bemrose-primary-school-in-the-east-midlands","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/from-the-ground-up-dig-into-their-first-co-design-with-bemrose-primary-school-in-the-east-midlands\/","title":{"rendered":"From The Ground Up\u00a0Dig into their First Co-design with Bemrose Primary School in the\u00a0East Midlands\u00a0"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4728 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-1536x1025.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-2048x1366.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/7038a0e2-adcd-4db6-b803-34ad24d6b619-187x125.jpg 187w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/683;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Photo: Shaun Taylor <\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This winter,&nbsp;<em>From&nbsp;The&nbsp;Ground Up&nbsp;Studio&nbsp;<\/em>invite the children of Bemrose Primary School to reimagine the landscapes of their future. Tasked with envisioning the world of 2050, the students will explore how we can revive both human and more-than-human communities, designing spaces where nature and people&nbsp;don\u2019t&nbsp;just coexist, but thrive together.&nbsp;We are thrilled to collaborate with&nbsp;<em>From&nbsp;The&nbsp;Ground Up<\/em>, a&nbsp;workers Co-operative&nbsp;studio dedicated to bridging the gap between people and the natural bio-systems we depend on.&nbsp;Their practice \u2013 built on the belief of fostering a culture celebrating a \u201cconstellation of things\u201d &#8211; repositions humans&nbsp;as the non-dominant force, in hopes to repair our relationship with the planet.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Brief: Reviving Human &amp; More-than-human Landscapes&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The studio\u2019s co-design brief, titled COMMONLAND, confronts a stark reality: the UK is now \u201cone of the most nature depleted countries on earth.\u201d Since 1970, we have lost 54% of the distribution of flowering plant species &#8211;&nbsp;plants vital to sustaining biodiversity.&nbsp;This decline is&nbsp;largely driven&nbsp;by intensive agricultural practices and the escalating effects of climate change.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Simultaneously, the demand for accessible green spaces has surged by 300% since the pandemic, highlighting a collective&nbsp;longing for connection with nature&nbsp;<em>(National Trust)<\/em>. The challenge posed by From&nbsp;The&nbsp;Ground Up is urgent yet hopeful:&nbsp;<em>How can children play a part in designing with natural bio-systems to&nbsp;benefit&nbsp;people, plants, and the planet?<\/em>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Over a series of workshops, students from Bemrose Primary will step into the role of landscape architects and ecologists. They will imagine a future where we need more wilderness, creatively intervening in local habitats to create places where both humans and the more-than-human world can flourish.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-stackable-image stk-block-image stk-block stk-6bf3612\" data-block-id=\"6bf3612\"><style>.stk-6bf3612 {margin-bottom:33px !important;}<\/style><figure><span class=\"stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"stk-img wp-image-4764 lazyload\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62.jpg\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1601\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62.jpg 2400w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62-1536x1025.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62-2048x1366.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/CCAC_100226_web-62-187x125.jpg 187w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2400px) 100vw, 2400px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 2400px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2400\/1601;\" \/><\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The Bemrose school Yr-5&#8217;s digging like beavers. Photo: Shaun Taylor<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">With<em>\u00a0From\u00a0The\u00a0Ground Up<\/em>\u2019s\u00a0expertise\u00a0in participatory design, their guidance will help the children navigate the complexities of ecology and community need. By\u00a0centring\u00a0the voices of the next generation, the studio\u00a0commits to providing children with creative problem-solving skills that will aid them in\u00a0contributing positively to\u00a0their future.\u00a0We\u00a0very much\u00a0look forward to seeing how the students of Bemrose Primary respond to this brief.\u00a0\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"992\" height=\"618\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-17-at-14.57.35.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4729 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-17-at-14.57.35.png 992w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-17-at-14.57.35-300x187.png 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-17-at-14.57.35-768x478.png 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-17-at-14.57.35-321x200.png 321w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/02\/Screenshot-2026-02-17-at-14.57.35-200x125.png 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 992px) 100vw, 992px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 992px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 992\/618;\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>The Materials Store (2023) From The Ground Up&#8217;s re-use materials hub at Primary, Nottingham. It provides three bays for storing and reprocessing art materials, keeping them out of landfill.<\/em>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>This winter,\u00a0From\u00a0The\u00a0Ground Up studio invite the children of Bemrose Primary School to reimagine the landscapes of their future. Tasked with envisioning the world of 2050, the students will explore how we can revive both human and more-than-human communities.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":10,"featured_media":47